.TH VID-CLI 1 "2026-11-18" "vid-cli 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vid-cli \- search, play and download YouTube videos, and browse anime metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vid-cli
.RI [ options ]
.I QUERY
.RI | " URL"
.br
.B vid-cli
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B vid-cli
.RI [ options ]
.B \-c
.br
.B vid-cli
.B \-\-anime
.RI [ options ]
.I TITLE
.br
.B vid-cli
.BR \-h " | " \-V " | " \-U
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vid-cli
is a small terminal front end for
.BR yt-dlp (1)
and
.BR mpv (1).
Searches are performed by yt-dlp using its
.B ytsearch
pseudo-URL. Playback is delegated to mpv after yt-dlp resolves the stream.
A pasted YouTube video, playlist or channel URL is handled directly.
Playlists and channels open a multi-select menu; selected videos are
queued and played in order.
.PP
With no query, the program opens a startup page when standard input is a
terminal, or when
.B VID_CLI_EXTERNAL_MENU
is set to
.BR 1 .
The page shows the current quality, player and history count, then offers
YouTube search, anime search, history and quit. Without a terminal, no
query prints usage and exits with status 1.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-anime ,
metadata, trailers, per-episode links and official streaming links are read
from the public AniList GraphQL API. No other anime site is contacted. Anime
mode prints only AniList data, plays only YouTube episodes and trailers, and
opens only links that AniList marks as official. When
.B \-\-anime
is given without a title, the program prompts for one on a terminal; without
a terminal it prints usage and exits 1.
.PP
The program never updates itself and never installs software. It writes
only to the XDG state/cache directories, temporary files under the cache
directory, and the download directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quality " " LEVEL
Select 360, 480, 720, 1080,
.B best
or
.BR worst .
The default is
.BR 720 .
The value is mapped to a yt-dlp format string.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-audio
Audio only. mpv is started with
.BR \-\-no\-video ;
downloads use
.BR yt\-dlp " \-x".
Audio downloads require ffmpeg.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-download
Download instead of playing. Files go to
.B VID_CLI_DL_DIR
(default
.IR $HOME/Videos/vid-cli ).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-number " " N
Number of search results to request. The default is 15.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-continue
Show the history menu, newest first, and replay the selected item.
History entries can also reopen an anime information screen.
.TP
.BR \-\-subs [= LANG ]
Load subtitles when available. The default language is
.BR en .
Use
.B \-\-subs=fr
or
.B \-\-subs fr
to choose another language. If the query itself starts with a token that
looks like a language code, put
.B \-\-
before it. Subtitle files are downloaded by yt-dlp into the temporary
cache directory and passed to the player.
.TP
.BR \-\-sort " " MODE
Sort search results by
.BR relevance ,
.B date
or
.BR views .
The date mode uses the yt-dlp
.B ytsearchdate
filter. The views mode sorts on the client because YouTube search has
no views filter; a message says so.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-history
Do not write to the history file.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-vlc
Use VLC instead of mpv. The stream is resolved by yt-dlp, so all YouTube
access still goes through yt-dlp. For adaptive video, mpv receives the audio
URL with its audio-file option; VLC mode uses a single-file stream.
.TP
.B \-\-anime
Anime mode. The remaining argument is an anime title, searched on AniList.
On a terminal, a missing title is requested with a free-text prompt.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage, all flags and all environment variables, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-update
Print update instructions and exit. The script does not modify itself.
.TP
.B \-\-
End option parsing. Useful when a query begins with a hyphen.
.SH ANIME MODE
Searches AniList and displays matches as:
.IP
romaji title (English title) | format | episodes | season year | score
.PP
After a selection, an information screen shows the synopsis with HTML
stripped, genres, studio, status and the next airing episode converted
to local time. The action menu offers:
.IP "1." 4
Browse official episodes from AniList's
.B streamingEpisodes
list. YouTube episodes are played locally; links to licensed services
open in the browser. When AniList has no per-episode links, a message
points to the series-level links instead.
.IP "2." 4
Play the official trailer. Only trailers whose AniList site is YouTube
are played.
.IP "3." 4
Print and open the official streaming links returned by AniList
.RB ( type " == " STREAMING ).
.IP "4." 4
Search YouTube for official clips or promotional videos using the title
plus
.BR "official PV" .
.IP "5." 4
Quit.
.PP
AniList responses are cached for ten minutes under
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/vid-cli .
A 429 response is retried at most once, with a short delay: a numeric
Retry-After value of 30 seconds or less is honoured, and a missing or
non-numeric value defaults to 5 seconds. Longer limits are not retried.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VID_CLI_PLAYER
Player binary. The default is
.BR mpv .
A binary whose name contains
.B vlc
is driven in VLC mode.
.TP
.B VID_CLI_DL_DIR
Download directory. The default is
.IR $HOME/Videos/vid-cli .
.TP
.B VID_CLI_HIST_DIR
State directory for the history file. The default is
.IR ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/vid-cli .
.TP
.B VID_CLI_RESULTS
Default number of search results. The default is 15.
.TP
.B VID_CLI_EXTERNAL_MENU
Use rofi instead of fzf when set to
.BR 1 .
If rofi is missing, fzf is used and a warning is printed.
.TP
.B VID_CLI_YTDLP_ARGS
Extra arguments passed to yt-dlp, split on whitespace. Example:
.BR "\-\-limit\-rate 2M" .
Globbing is disabled before the split. The tool itself adds no login,
paywall, DRM or region workarounds.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, even to an empty value, ANSI colors are disabled. Colors are
also disabled when stdout is not a terminal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/vid-cli/
AniList response cache, cache stamps and temporary work directories.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/vid-cli/histfile
Tab-separated history: timestamp, mode, id-or-URL, title. Newest first,
capped at 500 lines.
.TP
.I $HOME/Videos/vid-cli/
Default download directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or the user cancelled a menu.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, bad option, or an unsupported URL.
.TP
.B 2
A required dependency is missing.
.TP
.B 3
Network or API failure, or playback/download failed.
.TP
.B 4
Nothing found.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B vid-cli
Open the startup page in a terminal.
.TP
.B vid-cli \-\-anime
Prompt for an anime title on a terminal.
.TP
.B vid-cli "lofi hip hop"
Search and play.
.TP
.B vid-cli \-q 720 \-a "jazz"
Audio-only playback, requesting a 720p video format is ignored for
audio.
.TP
.B vid-cli \-d \-\-subs "conference talk"
Download a video and its subtitles.
.TP
.B vid-cli "https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=..."
Expand a playlist and multi-select videos.
.TP
.B vid-cli \-c
Replay from history.
.TP
.B vid-cli \-\-anime "Cowboy Bebop"
Browse AniList metadata and official links.
.SH LEGAL
The user is responsible for complying with YouTube's Terms of Service
and with local copyright law. vid-cli is for personal use. It does not
host, mirror or redistribute any content. It does not bypass paywalls,
DRM, login walls or geographic restrictions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yt\-dlp (1),
.BR mpv (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR jq (1)
